meta {
  name: List Leads
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/leads?page=1&page_size=20
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  page_size: 20
  ~status: new
  ~search: John
  ~assigned_user_id:
  ~platforms: facebook,google
  ~org_ids: 474b7e97-1471-411b-a135-947e0527975a
  ~active_only: true
}

docs {
  Returns paginated leads for the authenticated org.
  Only active leads are returned by default (is_active = true).

  Each lead includes:
    - is_active: boolean — false if this row was superseded by a newer submission
    - superseded_by: UUID | null — points to the newer active lead that replaced this one

  To see superseded leads, query the DB directly or use a future admin filter.

  Filters:
    - org_ids: CSV of branch UUIDs. Honoured only for a caller whose
      `lms.leads.view` scope resolves to tenant/all (tenant_admin); anyone else
      is clamped to their own branch whatever they send. Such a caller's read
      runs under the tenant Postgres role so RLS does not pin it to the session
      branch.
    - active_only: 'true' excludes leads in a terminal stage (converted /
      unqualified) in SQL. Used by the Bulk Assign screen. Only the literal
      strings 'true'/'false' are accepted.

  Rows are additionally scoped by the caller's `lms.leads.view` scope regardless
  of org_ids: own -> their own leads, team -> their reporting subtree (plus
  unassigned when rank allows), org/tenant -> the whole branch.
}
